from Clang Analyzer build step => https://gitlab.com/fhuberts/wireshark/-/pipelines/589120140

you can download artifacts if needed

for prototype warning, you need to add 

void proto_register_....(void);
void proto_reg_handoff_...(void);

on the top of file (look other dissector)

I am a little bit flummoxed why this got merged. Not because of the content, but because it breaks Windows builds. For whatever reason the Windows buildbot did not engage on this change, which is due to __attribute__ being used, as this is gcc specific.

There is a change at https://gitlab.com/wireshark/wireshark/-/merge_requests/7469 which I will fast-track, that simply removes the attribute, but @fhuberts my guess is, you might want to deal with that in !7467 otherwise the borders of that struct might not line up properly?

@crondaemon , @geraldcombs - any ideas, why the windows buildbots did not engage on this one?
